<p>For my friend Amy’s 23rd birthday, we headed to Hatchet Hall! They describe themselves as a Southern-inspired, Californian-influenced neighborhood restaurant, and I could definitely feel the influences from both those cuisines. The menu was adorable, and I’m so glad I got to try their famous Cast Iron Cornbread – I’m still dreaming of its beautifully caramelized exterior and soft, crumbly interior lined with shishito peppers. All with that butter…wow.</p>

